--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party content
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This distribution contains no vendored third-party source code. Runtime and
optional dependencies (mcp, numpy, httpx, hnswlib, fastembed) are installed
from PyPI under their own licenses and are not redistributed here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note on benchmark corpora (flagged, not resolved)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Apache-2.0 carries an express patent grant (Section 3) and a NOTICE
propagation requirement (Section 4(d)). Neither is affected by anything in this
file, but they constrain redistribution if third-party data is ever bundled.

`bench/` currently references external benchmark corpora (NFCorpus, SciDocs,
SciFact qrels) by name and expects them to be supplied separately by whoever
runs the benchmarks. If any such corpus is ever vendored into `bench/`, its
terms must be checked for compatibility with Apache-2.0 *before* it is
committed. Some corpora carry non-commercial or share-alike terms that are
incompatible with Apache-2.0 redistribution, and vendoring one would place
the whole distribution at risk rather than just that data file.

This is recorded as a known open question, deliberately unresolved. Resolving
it requires a maintainer decision plus a per-corpus license review, not a
packaging change.
